#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364765 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a64d73a-2983-5d05-9aa0-4582b2e7aee1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartic Polynomial Given Four Real Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cb3dc6f-9e9a-5cfd-a2ca-3f949c021a39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}-5{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+4x-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364767} {:answer/id #uuid "178989a3-9656-57c3-9bda-e2420ecfbb97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-12x-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364768} {:answer/id #uuid "1548c140-9073-5d74-9d62-14488dea1e51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}+3{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+12x-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364769} {:answer/id #uuid "40430b41-6818-5e43-97bd-4477b699b5c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}+5{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+12x-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364770} {:answer/id #uuid "b64d48ef-c2e6-54c6-8ce5-e457e3fed5a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}-5{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+4x-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364771}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b64d48ef-c2e6-54c6-8ce5-e457e3fed5a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}-5{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+4x-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364771} :answer-field/id #uuid "98fcae6b-0ca7-5a5c-b492-33e1b4bef326" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364766}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "40acc59f-8823-5531-95a7-abbc1303ec56" :question/math-academy-id "q-105752" :question/problem "The quartic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=2,$ and ${x}_{4}=-1$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $1.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quartic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=2,$ and ${x}_{4}=-1,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) & =1(x-2)(x-2)(x-2)(x-(-1)) \\\\  & =1(x-2)(x-2)(x-2)(x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1(x-2)(x-2)(x-2)(x+1) & =1({x}^{2}-4x+4)({x}^{2}-x-2) \\\\  & =1({x}^{4}-{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+8x+4{x}^{2}-4x-8) \\\\  & =1({x}^{4}-5{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+4x-8) \\\\  & ={x}^{4}-5{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+4x-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)={x}^{4}-5{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+4x-8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364772 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a64d73a-2983-5d05-9aa0-4582b2e7aee1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartic Polynomial Given Four Real Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25a15d76-4e4e-599a-b666-f0d8aaa86456" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^4-5x^3-9x^2+81x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364774} {:answer/id #uuid "9333a3cf-f9dc-51f0-be60-a22d5bb41b15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^4-5x^3+9x^2+81x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25a15d76-4e4e-599a-b666-f0d8aaa86456" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^4-5x^3-9x^2+81x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364774} :answer-field/id #uuid "47bddf47-4766-57e7-a6c8-43b860bb9e1a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364773}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ce6d5672-8e16-543e-bdf1-e22bd2d09c2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-319855" :question/problem "The quartic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=3,$ and ${x}_{4}=-4$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $1.$ Determine the **expanded form** of $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,108$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quartic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=3,$ and ${x}_{4}=-4,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) & =1(x-3)(x-3)(x-3)(x-(-4)) \\\\  & =(x-3)(x-3)(x-3)(x+4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)(x-3)(x-3)(x+4) & =({x}^{2}-6x+9)({x}^{2}+x-12) \\\\  & ={x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-6{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+72x+9{x}^{2}+9x-108 \\\\  & ={x}^{4}-5{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+81x-108.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)={x}^{4}-5{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+81x-108.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364776 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eda5034-e8a8-5260-8dc0-6c663880fe9e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartic Polynomial Given Two Real and Two Complex Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c7cad9f-bea4-593e-97b7-4e71ed4be833" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^4+74x^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c7cad9f-bea4-593e-97b7-4e71ed4be833" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^4+74x^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364778} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cb35c7d-18c8-52f7-ad41-3fcf23b6b6af" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364777}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "497c280e-c744-5ef7-8ff0-f0aa5098f06b" :question/math-academy-id "q-320185" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/assets/6a39af16798593716291ab84bfff4460279420f493bd10959782312187f0bf44.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Determine the **expanded form** of $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $2.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,72$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1,2}=\\pm \\text{i}$ and ${x}_{3,4}=\\pm 6\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=2.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =2(x-(-\\text{i}))(x-\\text{i})(x-(-6\\text{i}))(x-6\\text{i}) \\\\  & =2(x+\\text{i})(x-\\text{i})(x+6\\text{i})(x-6\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+\\text{i})(x-\\text{i})(x+6\\text{i})(x-6\\text{i}) & = \\\\ 2({x}^{2}+(\\text{i}-\\text{i})x-{\\text{i}}^{2})({x}^{2}+(6\\text{i}-6\\text{i})x-36{\\text{i}}^{2}) & = \\\\ 2({x}^{2}+1)({x}^{2}+36) & = \\\\ 2({x}^{4}+36{x}^{2}+{x}^{2}+36) & = \\\\ 2({x}^{4}+37{x}^{2}+36) & = \\\\ 2{x}^{4}+74{x}^{2}+72 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=2{x}^{4}+74{x}^{2}+72.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364779 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eda5034-e8a8-5260-8dc0-6c663880fe9e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartic Polynomial Given Two Real and Two Complex Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab1d19fe-4d08-593d-ab6f-1d84988a44ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^4+4x^3+14x^2+36x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364781} {:answer/id #uuid "24862d33-25bb-5eae-b440-cf71cbdbe9fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^4+4x^3+14x^2-36x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364782}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24862d33-25bb-5eae-b440-cf71cbdbe9fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^4+4x^3+14x^2-36x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364782} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3bba291-4c9a-5b75-9888-645ba747b77a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364780}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dd0f01ce-b194-5637-b280-44af6aaf3b75" :question/math-academy-id "q-320235" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/assets/4f960f00fbcbde79dee3603112ed08e8c34cf87b3ccbe781ee5acbf61a4482fd.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Determine the **expanded form** of $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $2.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,52$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1,2}=-2\\pm 3\\text{i},$ and ${x}_{3,4}=1\\pm \\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=2.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =2(x-(-2+3\\text{i}))(x-(-2-3\\text{i}))(x-(1+\\text{i}))(x-(1-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x-(-2+3\\text{i}))(x-(-2-3\\text{i}))(x-(1+\\text{i}))(x-(1-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 2({x}^{2}+4x+4+9)({x}^{2}-2x+1+1) & = \\\\ 2({x}^{2}+4x+13)({x}^{2}-2x+2) & = \\\\ 2({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+4{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+8x+13{x}^{2}-26x+26) & = \\\\ 2({x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-18x+26) & = \\\\ 2{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}+14{x}^{2}-36x+52 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=2{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}+14{x}^{2}-36x+52.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364783 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eda5034-e8a8-5260-8dc0-6c663880fe9e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartic Polynomial Given Two Real and Two Complex Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfaaeea3-8c70-59df-85f3-3441ac232cb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x^4+9x^3-6x^2-30x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bfaaeea3-8c70-59df-85f3-3441ac232cb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x^4+9x^3-6x^2-30x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364785} :answer-field/id #uuid "a16b129c-a174-512f-9699-7965f42e6c29" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364784}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a5bb48ac-20d2-5788-87bd-29b100a29b49" :question/math-academy-id "q-320276" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/assets/58136b4140d772431a823b66b03ebfa95bd51816e4df9be7f2401c29c97a5495.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Determine the **expanded form** of $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $3.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,36$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-3,$ ${x}_{2}=2,$ and ${x}_{3,4}=-1\\pm \\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=3.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =3(x-(-3))(x-2)(x-(-1+\\text{i}))(x-(-1-\\text{i})) \\\\  & =3(x+3)(x-2)(x-(-1+\\text{i}))(x-(-1-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+3)(x-2)(x-(-1+\\text{i}))(x-(-1-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{2}-2x+3x-6)({x}^{2}-x(-1-\\text{i})-x(-1+\\text{i})+(-1+\\text{i})(-1-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{2}+x-6)\\,({x}^{2}+2x+2) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+2x-6{x}^{2}-12x-12) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{4}+3{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-10x-12) & = \\\\ 3{x}^{4}+9{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-30x-36 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=3{x}^{4}+9{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-30x-36.$"}]}
